cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use mrtsp_exploration_ros2 in your research, please cite
  this software using the metadata below and specify the version
  or commit used. Please also cite the method it implements
  (Liu et al., 2025), listed under references.
type: software

title: >-
  mrtsp_exploration_ros2: A ROS 2 Implementation of Real-Time Map
  Optimization and MRTSP-Based Frontier Exploration

authors:
  - family-names: "Güler"
    given-names: "Mert"
    affiliation: "Yıldız Technical University"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0006-6709-7179"

version: "1.0.0"

license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/mertgulerx/mrtsp_exploration_ros2"
url: "https://github.com/mertgulerx/mrtsp_exploration_ros2"

abstract: >-
  mrtsp_exploration_ros2 is a standalone ROS 2 Jazzy exploration node
  that implements the method of Liu et al. (2025), "Enhancing autonomous
  exploration for robotics via real time map optimization and improved
  frontier costs". The node subscribes to the occupancy grid and the
  Nav2 global costmap, optimizes the map in real time with bilateral
  filtering and dilation, extracts frontiers with wavefront frontier
  detection on the optimized map, and computes frontier costs with the
  paper's equations. It builds a Minimum Ratio Traveling Salesman
  Problem (MRTSP) cost matrix, orders the frontiers greedily and sends
  the first frontier to Nav2 through NavigateToPose, then replans as the
  map grows until no frontier remains. The package does not depend
  on any other exploration framework and can be used in any
  Nav2-based stack. It is an independent implementation written from
  the paper, not the authors' code.

keywords:
  - autonomous exploration
  - mobile robotics
  - frontier-based exploration
  - occupancy grid maps
  - map optimization
  - bilateral filtering
  - wavefront frontier detection
  - minimum ratio traveling salesman problem
  - Nav2
  - ROS 2

